        "original_id": "ec06ffcf-3205-53f5-bf88-e2679396a2e2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Son of a Gun (EP), Incesticide, Sliver, In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety, In Utero\n- People: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, Dave Grohl\n- Companies: DGC\n- Organizations: The Vaselines, Nirvana\n- Places: Glasgow\n- Topics: compilation albums, tribute albums, cover songs\n\nFacts:\n- Son of a Gun is the debut EP single by the Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\n- Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\n- In 1992, DGC re-released the song \"Sliver\" to radio to support Nirvana's rarities compilation album Incesticide.\n- At the time of Incesticide's release, most of its material was already circulating in fan communities in lower quality.\n- Because Incesticide compiled songs from different recording sessions and periods without a stable Nirvana lineup, it featured four drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\n- The Son of a Gun EP title track reached a wider audience after Nirvana covered it, along with \"Molly's Lips,\" on the compilation album Incesticide.\n- In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety is a tribute album by various artists to Nirvana's 1993 third and final album In Utero.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eae2d181-f4d2-5fa7-ab52-a25be8e22f99",
        "text": "Page: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: Son of A Gun is the debut extended play single by Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\nPage: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: The title-song of this EP came to a wider audience after Nirvana covered it, along with \"Molly's Lips\", on their compilation album \"Incesticide\".\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: At the time, the majority of the material on \"Incesticide\" was circulating within fan communities (albeit in lower quality).\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Since the songs were recorded in different sessions and some were recorded when Nirvana did not have a stable formation, the album includes recordings by four different drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\nPage: Sliver (song). Sentence: DGC re-released the song to radio to support the release of the rarities compilation album \"Incesticide\" in 1992.\nPage: In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety. Sentence: In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety is a tribute album to Nirvana's 1993 third and final album, \"In Utero\", by various artists.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
